title    Seven Eighths Fusion (groove revision)
composer Claude
about    A 4-bar fusion loop in 7/8, phrased 2+2+3, over Dm11, Bbmaj13#11, Gm9 and an altered A7. Revised for groove only.

# Revision note. Feedback: "fusion 7 feels lame. keep everything, just the
# groove". Read as: the parts, harmony, voicings, tempo, and 2+2+3 phrasing
# stay, and only the rhythmic feel changes. In the original every part hit
# the same three group starts (steps 0, 4, 8) on a straight eighth grid, the
# hat had no sixteenth motion, and the drums repeated one bar three times, so
# the loop sounded stiff and square. What changed:
#   - light sixteenth swing (0.1) so the sixteenth grid breathes
#   - hats in sixteenths with ghost notes, accents still on 0, 4, 8
#   - snare backbeat on beats 3 and 6 of 7 (steps 4 and 10) with ghost notes,
#     the classic 2+2+3 backbeat, instead of one backbeat per bar
#   - kick syncopated (step 3 pushes into the snare, step 13 pushes into the
#     next bar) and varied between bars
#   - bass in sixteenths with ghost pickups and octave pops, and a chromatic
#     C#2 approach into the D at the loop point
#   - keys comp moved off the group starts (steps 0, 3, 9, 12) so it answers
#     the kick and snare instead of doubling them, and A7alt is pushed a
#     sixteenth early in bar 4
# Unchanged: tempo, meter, every keys voicing, the pad, the crash, voices.

# Tempo: quarter = 120, so the eighth-note beat is 240. Seven eighth beats
# with 2 steps each gives 14 sixteenth steps per bar, grouped 2+2+3 eighths =
# 4+4+6 steps (group starts at steps 0, 4, 8).
tempo    240
beats    7
steps    2
swing    0.1

voice keys epiano vol=0.75 pan=-0.25
voice pad strings vol=0.35 pan=0.3
voice bass ebass vol=0.95
voice kick kick vol=0.95
voice snare snare vol=0.8
voice hat hat vol=0.55
voice crash crash vol=0.6

pattern A
# Keys: same voicings as the original, new rhythm. Hits on steps 0, 3, 9, 12
# sit between the kick (0, 8) and snare (4, 10) so the comp interlocks with
# the drums. Bar 4 lands A7alt on step 7, a sixteenth before the 3-group.
keys | F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4-- .- . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4-? . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- | A3+D4+E4+G4- . A3+D4+E4+G4-- .- . A3+D4+E4+G4-? . A3+D4+E4+G4- | Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4-- .- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4-? . Bb3+D4+F4+A4- | Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4-- . G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5!------ |
# Pad: unchanged.
pad  | E5+A5------------- | -------------- | -------------- | -------- F5+Bb5----- |
# Bass: root on each group start as before, now with sixteenth ghost pickups
# (step 3, 9), octave pops (step 7), and a 7-to-5 run in the 3-group. Bar 4
# walks A1 E2 G2 and ends on C#2, a half step under the D2 at the loop point.
bass | D2- . D2? A2- . D3? D2 . D2? C3- A2 | Bb1- . Bb1? F2- . Bb2? Bb1 . Bb1? A2- F2 | G1- . G1? D2- . G2? G1 . G1? F2- D2 | G1- . G1? D2- . G2? A1-! . E2 G2 C#2? |
# Drums: kick on 0 and 8 (the 2-group and 3-group starts), snare backbeat on
# 4 and 10, sixteenth hats. Bars 1 and 3 push with kick on 3 and 13; bar 2
# answers with kick on 6; bar 4 ends with a snare fill into the loop.
kick  | x..x .... x....x | x... ..x. x..x.. | x..x .... x....x | x..x .... x.x... |
snare | .o.. X.o. .oX.o. | .o.. X..o .oX..o | .o.. X.o. .oX.o. | .o.. X.o. .oXoXX |
hat   | Xoxo Xoxo Xoxoxo | Xoxo Xoxo Xoxox. | Xoxo Xoxo Xoxoxo | Xoxo Xoxo Xo.... |
crash | X... .... ...... | _ | _ | _ |

loop A
